OUT=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent;ROOT=OUT.parent;SOURCE=ROOT/'gutenberg-first-prose-https-targets-v1';proposal=ROOT/'gutenberg-first-prose-cohort-proposal-v1/proposal.json';rows=json.loads(proposal.read_text())['records'];sha=lambda x:hashlib.sha256(x).hexdigest()
notes={
58940:('The great, round moon looked down','1878 Beadle & Adams copyright notice; Dime Library vol.IV no.49; US imprint.','Historic English novel attributed on title page to Albert W.Aiken. Positive retained1878 English publication context supports original-English candidacy; originalissue scan not collated.','Modern front/tail transcription instructions, illustrations and captions, extensive Beadle publishercatalogs. Tail notes explicitly report inserting “critter,” said” from another version: targeted source-fidelity/version dependency. Mechanical correction credit does not itself copyright the whole old body.','Novel ending THE END precedes ads and modernnotes. Keep all illustration-dependent text decisions separate; prejudicial portrayals are visible in opening and require semantic review.'),
65415:('By the fragment of a log-book','Undated George Routledge and Sons/London and E.P.Button/NewYork imprint as captured; no guessed editionyear.','Author-attributed English introduction explains assembling the story from history/tradition/manuscript and title names JamesGrant. Historical English edition supports candidacy; originalpublicationlanguage not independently collated.','Original-style narrative introduction BEFORE contents; verse epigraphs and historical Notes at end; no modern creative introduction identified in reviewed front/tail.','Capture full introduction+TOC before ChapterI prose. Do not lose authorintroduction or quotedepigraph/notes as accidental boilerplate; include original notes as dependent reference component.'),
52126:('So many of my dreams have come true','James Nisbet &Co London1889; signed English dedication JamesRunciman May1,1889.','Signed contemporaneous English dedication and author/title/imprint are positive source support beyond native en metadata.','Dedication, illustrationcaptions, narrative booksI/II, author-signed AppendixA, organizational Mission AppendixB, publishercatalog at end.','Candidate narrative ends before AppendixA, but appendices are separate retained historical components, not modernjunk by default. Firstappendix signedRunciman; organizationalreport has separate contributor scope.'),
3028:('THIS was Mrs. Peterkin.','Second-edition preface in retainedsource; exact printimprint/year not captured.','Authorattributed secondedition preface discusses earlier YoungFolks/StNicholas English storypublication and “The Peterkins at the Farm.” Positive source publicationhistory, not just en.','Dedication and secondedition preface, apparently integral authorial narrative framing, plus modern Producedby lines.','Prose starts after THE LADY WHO PUT SALT IN HER COFFEE heading; authorial preface remains separately retained, no automatic deletion authorized.'),
59366:('Throughout the length and breadth of this London','Routledge London/NewYork NewEdition1867; JohnChilds printers. Exact sourcePDFURL and Emory/WebArchive identifier retained in transcriber note.','Named EdmundYates English novel in1867 English imprint gives positive publicationcontext; exactfirstpublicationlanguage not independently collated.','Modern Producedby and source-scan note; dedication, contents and printercolophon are distinct from novel.','Candidate mainprose THE END before printercolophon; no added moderncreative essay identified in fullfrontmatter/tail.'),
34616:('A very central place is Newmanham','Undated Dick &Fitzgerald NewYork titlepage; Kentuckiana DigitalLibrary credited for scans.','English author-attributed novel; narrator explicitly describes himself as a bornBriton. Supports English-authorial voice, does not by itself prove originalpublicationlanguage or exact printyear.','Modern productioncredits, titlepage, originalpublisher advertisements after THE END.','Mainprose boundary before NEW WORKS IN PRESS; printedcatalog is not novel continuation.'),
21555:('It was in the autumn of the year 1828','Exactprintedition not identified. Modern NickHodson note asserts original1845 and transcription1998/reformatting2003/2005; distinguish claim from printscan evidence.','ChapterOne English narrative is attributed to CaptainFrederickMarryat; modern introductory originalpublicationclaim provides lead, not independent firstedition proof.','IDENTIFIED ADDED MODERN PROSE: biography/appraisal beginning CaptainFrederickMarryat was born... through This e-text was transcribed... inside PG START. Separate this addition from historic narrative.','Exclude modernbio from any future originalbody derivative by explicit offsets; do not quarantine Marryat story merely because a modern transcriber is credited.'),
22845:('Three years ago, Hannah Colson was','No historical printimprint/editionyear in reviewed retainedfrontmatter; PG credited DavidWidger.','Source explicitly titles and attributes the English story to MaryRussellMitford; exact originalprint/publicationlanguage provenance still to establish.','Modern Producedby line, title/author frontmatter, embedded literary footnote and legacy PGendcreditline.','Keep embedded authorial/literaryfootnote dependency; legacy PGendline is packaging. No creative modernintro identified in fullfrontmatter/tail.'),
31489:('"Leone," cried a loud voice','Undated Donohue,Henneberry &Co Chicago titlepage. PGheader CharlotteM.Brame; titlepage BerthaM.Clay.','CapturedPGagent explicitly includes alias Clay,BerthaM.; titlepage/header difference reconciles to captured authorityalias, not evidence by itself of wrongauthor. Exactedition/authorship history not independently collated.','Productioncredits and titlepage; no separate moderncreativeintro found in reviewedregions.','Retain alias linkage in family/provenance and do not silently relabel titlepage author. Unknownprintyear and potential pseudonym attribution require source-specific review, no automatic contradiction claim.'),
2521:('When Death is present in a household','PGsource statement:1896 Smith,Elder &Co edition transcribed by DavidPrice.','Named ElizabethGaskell Englishstory tied by retainedtranscriptionstatement to English1896 edition; originalpublicationlanguage history not separately checked.','Modern transcriptionline/contact followed by title/author and ChapterI; narrative includes quoted Biblical/literary passages.','Candidatebody starts at ChapterI prose; sourceedition/contactnotice stays in provenance, not story. Moderntranscription alone is no blanket rightsbar.'),
6705:('The daughter of Mary Wollstonecraft and Godwin','1890 title/date; signedpreface LucyMadoxRossetti. CWRU digitalimages credited.','Signed1890 Englishpreface directly describes authorialresearch/writing; strong source support for original-English authorship.','Authorpreface acknowledges earlier researchers and permission for MaryShelley letters; letters/documents are embedded thirdparty historical components, not proof of modernadditions.','Preserve quotation/letter attribution and preface separately; no basis to mark everyhistorical quotation newlycopyrighted or omit dependencies.'),
2317:('The story of my heart commences seventeen years ago','No printimprint/date captured; PGupdated2026 and SusanL.Farley credit are digitizationmetadata, not new originalbody authorship.','Title names RichardJefferies and original autobiographical firstperson Englishvoice; printsource/firstpublicationlanguage not independently established.','Illustrationplaceholder, title, contents; no added creative modernessay or tailnote found in reviewedregions.','Narrative12chapters; modern release/update dates must not replace historic workdate.'),
10141:('The life of him in honor of whose memory','NewYork printed forSociety MDCCCLXX; delivery May17,1870.','Contemporaneous title and meetingminutes identify Bryant delivering this Englishdiscourse to NewYorkHistoricalSociety; positive originaloral/publicationcontext.','Meetingresolution signedrecordingsecretary AndrewWarner, officerslist, printercolophon distinct from Bryantdiscourse; historical quotedmaterial in discourse not exhaustively inventoried.','Candidate speech excludes Societyminutes/roster and EVENING POST printerline; preserve all sourceparatext/attributions outside candidate.'),
8530:('This book was not designed as a biography','No printimprint/year in frontmatter. Titlepage GeorgeParsonsLathrop; PGproductionteam credits.','Firstperson authorial explanation of purpose/research and named title support original-English critical work; firstedition metadata not independently resolved.','Illustrationplaceholder, contents; three historicalappendices and backindex, embedded footnotes/documentextracts.','Mainchapters end before actualAPPENDIXI (not TOCmention). Appendices are retained separate historicalsourcecomponents, not automatically discarded modernnotes. Preserve footnote/crossreference dependencies.'),
3120:('One of the worst characteristics of modern fiction','No originalimprint/year in frontmatter; PGcredits DavidWidger.','Named CharlesDudleyWarner Englishcriticalessay discussing British/American fiction; originalpublicationlanguage not independently established from currentedition.','Short producer/title/author frontmatter; quoted criticism includes Heine wording and historicalliterary references.','No added moderncreative essay identified. Original essayquotations still need attribution/dependency preservation.'),
48959:('WE sat late on the verandah','Chatto &Windus London1896.','Named GrantAllen English1896 edition with Englishnatureessayvoice and contemporaneousimprint supports original-English candidacy.','Frontandbackpublishercatalogs, dedication/illustrations, quotation of GeorgeMeredith in opening, moderntail TRANSCRIBER NOTES reporting typo correction.','Body THE END precedes printer/catalog/modernnotes. Existingquotation is historicalthirdparty component; no automaticrights decision from its author being absent metadata.'),
60193:('On the roof of the ruined church','JohnLane BodleyHead London/NewYork1896.','Author/title/imprint plus Englishtravelvignettes give positive historicalEnglishpublicationcontext. Substantial Frenchquoted dialogue visible; originalEnglish origin is distinct from everywindow being English.','Epigraph, TOC, integral Sidenote vignetteheadings, historicalpublishercatalog, modernTRANSCRIBER’S NOTES.','Candidate body through FINIS before illustratedprinter+catalog. Side notes carry sectiontitles/dates; do not treat allbracketed text as removable. Frenchdialogue must survive exactsourceandlanguage assessment.'),
60951:('The brave man is the elder son of creation','Body signed HenryD.Thoreau,July1840; no printimprint/year captured.','Signed dated Englishessay at end provides positive authorialsourceevidence beyond en metadata.','Contents, LatinVirgil epigraph/Englishrendering, quotedverse integrated into argument. No separate moderncreativeintro found.','Keep signature/date and quotedepigraph/verse attribution as explicit components; languagewindows maysee Latinquote, no overrideauthorized.'),
3144:('THERE appeared a few years since','RetainedPGtranscriptionstatement:1890 Macmillan PlaysandPuritans collection. Footnote cites original NorthBritishReview no.LI November1856.','Contemporary Englishreviewpublication citation plus namedKingsley and Englishcollection is positive original-English publicationcontext. It is a review of Froude, not Froude’s wholehistory.','Modern transcriptioncontact, articleheading with footnoteref{219}, original FOOTNOTES {219}/{246}.','Footnotes identify source/context and must remain available to article; do not cut them just to yield pureprose. Historical/polemical claims not factcleared.'),
7881:('Hotel de Louvre, January 6th, 1858.','RetainedVOL.I/VOL.II notebook compilation; no exacthistoricalprintimprint/year captured.','Named Hawthorne Englishfirstperson traveljournals: French/Italian refer to places, not blankettranslation. Source-Englishauthorialvoice positive; exact published compilation/editor identity unresolved.','EIGHT explicit --ED. bracketannotations detected/read, including substantial personal commentary and editorialbridge. Editor not listed in cohort creator-only metadata: concrete missingcomponentprovenance.','Do not silently attribute editor’s prose to Hawthorne or delete bracketnotes indiscriminately. Preserve all8exactnotes and chronology dependencies; resolve historicaleditor/edition or explicitly separate components before derivative.'),
}
end_rules={58940:r'^THE END\.\r?\n',52126:r'^[ \t]*\*APPENDIX A\.\*',59366:r'^THE END\.\r?\n',34616:r'^THE END\.\r?\n',21555:r'^THE END\.\r?\n',22845:r"^End of Project Gutenberg's The Beauty",31489:r'^THE END\.\r?\n',10141:r'^EVENING POST, 41 Nassau',8530:r'^APPENDIX I\.\r?\n',48959:r'^[ \t]*THE END\.\r?\n',60193:r'^[ \t]*FINIS\r?\n'}
